[2026-11-23T08:04:24.908Z] [INFO]       "output": "Honor the pinned manager package version for SSH maintenance\n\nA 2.48.0 operator CLI sends its own Bash program via `--host`, but packaged maintenance follows the SSH host's `hive-manager`/ `hive` installation (without checking its package version) or falls back to npm on that host. The invoking shell's `HIVE_MANAGER_PACKAGE_VERSION` is not carried in the remote command. This lets the wrapper and storage/reporting implementation have different versions. See [remote dispatch and package fallback](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/v2.48.0/src/hive-manager/cli.sh#L117-L189).\n\nTo reproduce on a disposable OpenSSH target with Node and npm and no Hive Mind package on its noninteractive PATH, invoke `HIVE_MANAGER_PACKAGE_VERSION=2.48.0 /path/to/pinned/hive-manager --host STAGE deploy disk --help`. Put a test npm shim after Node's bin directory that records argument boundaries and exits without network access. The remote exec requests `@link-assistant/hive-mind@latest`. With a different installed package that has the storage module on the target PATH, dispatch prefers that package even with an explicit local fallback pin. Local unstreamed invocation from the pinned package uses its own installed module.\n\nPlease carry an explicit package pin across SSH, verify an installed package against it before dispatch, and expose the effective package/version in diagnostics. Keep the shipped CLI/image and container-side version semantics explicit in the runbook. The migration currently installs the exact target package and checks its PATH acquisition separately.\n\nMigration context is link-assistant/hive-mind-control-center#1 and link-assistant/hive-mind-control-center#2.\n\n\n__formal_ai_exit=0\n",
[2026-11-23T08:04:24.908Z] [INFO]       "title": "gh issue view 'https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/4135' --json title --jq .title && echo && gh issue view 'https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/4135' --json body --jq .body; printf '\n__formal_ai_exit=%s\n' $?",
[2026-11-23T08:04:24.908Z] [INFO]       "metadata": {
