[2026-11-23T08:04:47.926Z] [INFO]         "preview": "00001| # Hive Mind Manager\n00002| \n00003| `hive-manager` runs on a local deployment host, over SSH from a developer machine, and inside Hive Mind images. It ships with `@link-assistant/hive-mind`. To use a single copy without installing the package, download the script or stream it into Bash.\n00004| \n00005| ```bash\n00006| npm install -g @link-assistant/hive-mind\n00007| hive-manager --help\n00008| \n00009| curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/main/src/hive-manager/cli.sh | bash\n00010| curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/main/src/hive-manager/cli.sh | bash -s -- deploy --help\n00011| ```\n00012| \n00013| For interactive commands, redirects, or repeated use, save the file and invoke it with Bash. Replace `main` with a release reference or commit SHA to pin the download. Bash and standard Linux utilities are enough for deployment preparation and local backup. Docker operations also require a local Docker Engine on the deployment host and permission to access it. Install Node.js and Hive Mind to run package maintenance commands on the host, or use `deploy` to run them inside the image. When a standalone maintenance command is missing locally and npm is available, the manager uses `npm exec` with the published package. Set `HIVE_MANAGER_PACKAGE_VERSION` to pin that fallback.\n00014| \n00015| ## JavaScript library\n00016| \n00017| Install `@link-assistant/hive-mind` in your project and import the public `@link-assistant/hive-mind/hive-manager` entry point from Node.js 24 or later. The package includes TypeScript declarations. Importing the entry point runs no commands, writes no files, and produces no output.\n00018| \n00019| ```js\n00020| import { HiveManagerError, previewTaskRecordRepair } from '@link-assistant/hive-mind/hive-manager';"
